cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EXCISE: Query-Side Exclusion for Late-Interaction Retrieval"
message: "If you use this software, the benchmark, or the released checkpoints, please cite the paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ali
    given-names: Mohammed
    affiliation: "University of Innsbruck"
  - family-names: Abdallah
    given-names: Abdelrahman
    affiliation: "University of Innsbruck"
  - family-names: Jatowt
    given-names: Adam
    affiliation: "University of Innsbruck"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohammedAli9330/EXCISE"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A frozen late-interaction index scores every query token by its best document match at the same
  sign, so naming what a user does not want promotes it. EXCISE detects the excluded topic, re-embeds
  only the shortlist at query time, and subtracts a penalty on that topic. The index is never rebuilt.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - late interaction
  - ColBERT
  - negation
  - exclusion
